// Coverage: M3 opening checklist (unit M3-P18, 2026-09-25).
//   "Your 2026 at a glance" (TaxSection::Checklist = 38; SaveChecklist/EstimateChecklist with the
//   shared M1 Save-variant block, every #[libertas_next_response] list gains SaveChecklist) is the
//   page after the people pages: first_open/rank/reached place it between the children page and
//   the income hub, whose previous it becomes (before_income; before_checklist is the last people
//   page); progress now counts 11 sections (12 with dependents), the checklist 3 (4), income 4 (5)
//   and so on; the review's answers gain "Your 2026 at a glance  N topics" ("None of these").
//   Checklist (federal_model.rs) holds six Bitflags u32 questions in the plain-struct catalog form
//   (IncomeTopics 9 flags, AdjustmentTopics 6, DeductionTopics 8, CreditTopics 3, OtherTaxTopics
//   4, PaymentTopics 2, each with a zero "None of these") and whole_return (a seventh Bitflags,
//   WholeReturnTopics 5, since gate fixes batch A; it was a bool). The page opens by
//   EditRequest with every tick computed (checklist_value: the stored ticks | each flag's entries,
//   the FLAGS table's `entered`); Save stores every tick (walk-owned data: FederalDraft.checklist,
//   was `planned`, the ticks with nothing entered), records Checklist and refuses undeclared bits.
//   Walk-owned data replaced CHECKLIST_TOPIC_HAS_ENTRIES: a topic's entries are owned by its tick,
//   so unticking one removes them (FLAGS.clear), named first by the running estimate; every other
//   page keeps a topic with entries ticked (follow_ticks). Planned = ticked with nothing entered.
//   Deviation: the ticks are a Checklist, not the card's
//   Vec<TaxSection>: nine flags share a page (gifts and car loan the deductions page, Marketplace
//   and less-common credits More credits, four Other taxes flags, two payments flags), so a
//   section list could not reopen the ticks as ticked; planned_sections gives the sections.
//   Studio compile_schema checks every variant's `$.value` against each calculation's `$.value`
//   input, and MoreCredits.credits is a list, so the credits question is `credit_topics`.
//   Hubs (income, adjustments, itemized, credits): first row "What you told us" (told_us, section
//   Checklist; each hub's allowed_sections gains the checklist, which opened from a hub returns to
//   it); suggestion (hub_suggestion) = first offered topic with a remaining item other than a
//   planned one, else first planned-with-nothing-entered or derived topic in hub order (derived:
//   HSA, self-employed benefits, IRA hints; education, saver; unvisited itemized topics), else
//   Continue; the income hub's "Wages while empty" rule is gone. A planned topic with nothing
//   entered is listed "Not started" (with_checklist_rows). The deductions page opens on Compare
//   while unsaved after an itemizable tick (ITEMIZABLE: medical, taxes, mortgage, carryovers,
//   investment interest, less common). EstimateChecklist replies with the estimate and the planned
//   path, "Your return: Income, Deductions, Federal payments, Review" (checklist_path: a section
//   with a tick, an entry, a derived need or a remaining item; hub_of maps items to sections),
//   also the page's progress. M3-P16's fifth source (planned_items): each planned tick, "You told
//   us about <topic>; nothing is entered yet", on its page (an itemized topic on the deductions
//   page while not itemizing), blocking Finish. The "Gifts to charity" tick plans the deductions
//   page, which asks the cash gifts once as an amount (Deductions.cash_gifts, 0 is none; gate
//   fixes batch A replaced the None/Gave choice). STORAGE_FORMAT 40. Fixtures: M1 ticks W-2 wages and
//   interest (4 structure taps), M2 W-2 wages (3); 12 and 20 fields unchanged, one more Next each
//   (M1 13 requests, M2 12). Tests: src/tests/cross/interview.rs
//   checklist_follows_the_people_pages_and_opens_with_nothing_ticked, ticks_become_planned_topics,
//   topics_with_entries_open_ticked, undeclared_checklist_ticks_are_refused,
//   derived_topics_need_no_tick, hub_suggests_attention_then_planned_then_continue,
//   itemizable_ticks_open_deductions_on_compare, checklist_estimate_lists_the_planned_sections,
//   planned_topic_without_entries_is_a_remaining_item; sequence and fixture tests amended.
// Coverage: M3 guided walk, summaries and skipped sections (unit M3-P19, 2026-09-25).
//   TaxSection is declared in sequence order, each hub followed by its topics (Setup 0 .. Review
//   38, SEQUENCE's order), so a hub's popup reads the previous section, its topics, then the next
//   section (the checklist row and the credits hub's care row, which reopen earlier pages, sort
//   first); rank() is the discriminant (income by period ranks as payments). STORAGE_FORMAT 41
//   (TaxSection is stored in finished_sections). The walk (design (b) A'): walk_topics = a hub's
//   planned (planned_sections) or derived (derived_topics) topics not yet visited, in hub order;
//   enter(hub) opens its first one directly, else the hub. The sequence enters a hub through
//   next_page (checklist, deductions page), resume and Continue; a topic save returns through
//   enter, so it opens the next walk topic, else the hub; Back and Go to show the hub. The hub
//   whose walk has ended is the section summary: progress "... · You're done with income",
//   suggestion attention first, else Continue. Visited rule (the rediscovered gap: income and
//   adjustments topic saves recorded nothing): visit() records a topic in finished_sections when
//   it was planned or derived before the save (income, adjustments, the less-common pages;
//   itemized and credits topics already recorded); other saves record nothing, so an unchanged
//   Next stays unchanged. Derived: HSA only while an owner has box 12 W and no account (a stored
//   special answer is attention, not re-walked); itemized topics are walked only when planned
//   (M3-P9 walked every unvisited one), so hub_suggestion is attention, walk, next. Skipping:
//   sections_with_needs (shared with checklist_path) shows a section with a tick, an entry, a
//   derived topic or a remaining item (items of the return with income continued); the itemized
//   hub whenever the route itemizes; credits entries exclude the care row (answered on the people
//   page). skip_empty_sections runs in commit on every accepted change: from first_open, each
//   section with no need is recorded in finished_sections, in the same revision. Continue and
//   Back use next_shown/previous_shown (hub previous, allowed_sections' first and last entries,
//   the deductions, other taxes and payments pages' previous). The "Anything else?" page and
//   its walk step were retired in gate fixes batch A; the injured spouse page is the walked
//   section after payments while its tick is planned. Progress (progress_line) counts setup, you, people (with dependents), the
//   checklist, the shown sections, the page's own section and the review. Income hub rows carry
//   count and amount, "1 W-2 · $60,000.00" (topic_summary: the documents' previews; a business
//   shows the count only). Not done, reported: adjustments and credits rows keep their counts
//   without amounts; a section already recorded is not reopened when a later change gives it a
//   need (un-finishing it would lock every later page through reached()); the review's remaining
//   items and the hub attention cover that case. Fixtures: M1 6 requests (was 13), M2 6 (was
//   12); navigation taps 6 and 5 on 2 and 2 screens; 12 and 20 fields unchanged. Tests:
//   src/tests/cross/interview.rs m1_path_is_checklist_wages_interest_summary_review,
//   m2_path_skips_the_credits_hub, walk_follows_planned_topics_in_hub_order,
//   derived_hsa_and_education_are_walked_without_a_tick,
//   empty_sections_are_skipped_and_listed_on_the_review, a_section_with_attention_is_never_skipped,
//   revisit_from_the_hub_returns_to_it, progress_counts_only_shown_sections,
//   back_passes_skipped_sections, resume_opens_the_next_step, popup_lists_previous_topics_then_next;
